  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "We have two data points: multimodal (scvi_n200 + ViT-L, concat) at 0.532 acc and image-only (ViT-L) at 0.227 acc. The critical missing piece is the RNA-only baseline with the same scvi_n200 encoder and singleprofile setting. Config_003 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) completes the modality ablation: if RNA-only approaches 0.532, the image modality adds little and future effort should focus on RNA representation; if it is substantially lower, fusion is genuinely beneficial and we should invest in better fusion/aggregation. This single experiment resolves the most important uncertainty—whether the multimodal gain is driven by RNA alone or by true cross-modal synergy—before spending budget on more complex multiprofile or fusion variants."
}

